.TH HALCYON-GUI 1 "November 2026" "halcyon 0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
halcyon-gui \\- Qt 6 window for the Halcyon console
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B halcyon-gui
[\\fB\\-\\-url\\fR \\fIURL\\fR] [\\fB\\-\\-check\\fR] [\\fB\\-\\-send\\fR \\fITEXT\\fR]
[\\fB\\-\\-screenshot\\fR \\fIFILE\\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B halcyon-gui
is the station console as a native Qt 6 window: status rows, a pane showing the
receiver spectrum or the waterfall of the last burst, a transcript, and controls
for the profile, speed level, frequency, messages, link tests, the modem host
and Hermes Lite 2 discovery.  It is a client of
.BR halcyon (1)'s
loopback API, so the console must be running.
.PP
The package ships this window only where Qt 6 was available when it was built,
which in practice means a native build.  On architectures whose package was
cross-built, use
.BR halcyon-tui (1)
instead; it needs no display.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \\-\\-url " " \\fIURL\\fR
Console to attach to.  Defaults to \\fIhttp://127.0.0.1:8730\\fR.
.TP
.B \\-\\-check
Print the console state and exit without opening a window.
.TP
.BR \\-\\-send " " \\fITEXT\\fR
Send a message through the simulated channel and show what the console
decoded.
.TP
.BR \\-\\-screenshot " " \\fIFILE\\fR
Draw the window, save it as a PNG and exit.  On a machine without a display,
set \\fBQT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen\\fR.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HALCYON_URL
Console URL used when \\fB\\-\\-url\\fR is absent.
.TP
.B HALCYON_MYCALL
Call sign reported when the window starts the modem host.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR halcyon (1),
.BR halcyon-tui (1)
.SH AUTHOR
The Halcyon authors.
